# The world
Six countries share one world economy: {{ ([country] + others)|join(", ") }}. Money is in credits. Each quarter every leader moves once, one after another; the economy of the quarter is settled after all six have moved. You see what earlier leaders did this quarter and what they said in public, and you know who still moves after you.
- Five goods: {{ sectors|join(", ") }}. SERVICES cannot be stored. Every good is traded between countries. Buyers prefer cheaper goods, home goods, and sellers they trust.
- Tariffs make imports from a country dearer. A sanction blocks all trade between the two countries, both ways, and costs the sanctioning country some stability.
- Treaties: supply contracts, tariff caps, no-sanction pacts and loans. A treaty you offer must be accepted by the other side; an offer stays open until the end of the next quarter. Breaking a treaty (a tariff above an agreed cap, a sanction under a pact, cutting contracted supplies, missing a loan payment you could pay) ends it and makes every country trust you less.
- Trust between countries rises when treaties are kept and falls after violations and sanctions. Trust affects trade.
- Stability (0 to 100) falls with unemployment, inflation, food and energy shortages and sanctions you impose, and rises with welfare spending. When stability is very low there is unrest, and the leader can be removed.
- The government taxes household income, spends on welfare, military and subsidies, and borrows when the treasury runs out. Interest rises with debt. If debt grows too large compared with GDP, the country defaults: half the debt is written off, stability drops sharply, and for a while spending may not exceed revenue.
- Firms with few competitors charge more and hire less. Antitrust action and new firms reduce that power.
- Random events happen: harvest failures, energy disasters, industry collapses, epidemics, new discoveries, the death of a leader.

# Your actions (at most {{ max_actions }} per quarter)
Write each action EXACTLY in the shape shown: "type" plus only the fields listed for that type. Any other field makes the action invalid and it is not carried out.
Shared actions:
{% for name, help in shared %}
- {{ name }}: {{ help }}
{% endfor %}
Special powers of {{ country }}:
{% for name, help in special %}
- {{ name }}: {{ help }}
{% endfor %}
{% for n in notes %}
- {{ n }}
{% endfor %}
Countries: {{ ([country] + others)|join(", ") }}. Sectors and goods: {{ sectors|join(", ") }}.
Actions you do not list leave your current policies unchanged. Rates and shares are fractions (0.25 means 25%).

# Answer format
Answer with ONE JSON object with ALL nine fields below, in this order. Every field is required, even when a list is empty; never stop before "actions" and "forecast". Keep texts short.
Shape (types only):
{"situation_read": text, "facts_used": [{"country": NAME, "metric": METRIC, "value": number}], "predictions": [{"country": NAME, "move": MOVE, "probability": number}], "stance": {"power": number, "citizens": number, "world": number}, "private_plan": text, "public_statement": text, "commitments": [{"kind": KIND, "target": NAME, "turns": integer}], "actions": [{"type": ACTION, ...fields of that action}], "forecast": {"my_gdp_growth_pct": number, "my_stability_next": number}}
The fields:
- situation_read: your reading of the situation (at most {{ td.situation_read_max_chars }} characters)
- facts_used: up to {{ td.facts_used_max }} numbers from the briefing you rely on: {country, metric, value}; metric is one of gdp, gdp_growth_pct, inflation_pct, unemployment_pct, stability, debt_to_gdp, military, treasury, interest_rate_pct, wage
- predictions: for countries that still move after you this quarter: {country, move, probability 0 to 1}; move is one of status_quo, raise_tariff_on_me, sanction_me, cut_exports_to_me, offer_treaty_to_me, accept_my_treaty, break_treaty_with_me, cooperate_with_others; an empty list if nobody moves after you
- stance: {power, citizens, world}, how much weight you give to your country's power, your citizens' welfare and the rest of the world; three numbers from 0 to 1 that add up to 1
- private_plan: your plan, seen by nobody else (at most {{ td.private_plan_max_chars }} characters)
- public_statement: what you say to the world (at most {{ td.public_statement_max_chars }} characters)
- commitments: up to {{ td.commitments_max }} public promises: {kind, target, turns 1 to 4, max_rate for tariff_cap}; kind is one of no_tariff_increase, tariff_cap, no_sanction, no_export_cut, keep_treaty
- actions: up to {{ max_actions }} actions, each in the exact shape listed under "Your actions" (no other fields)
- forecast: {my_gdp_growth_pct, my_stability_next}: your forecast for {{ country }} next quarter
